          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\omega)
            and given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"} Hamiltonian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \colon X \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebra of functions
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+space"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space"} path space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [I,X]
            – the “space of histories” or “space of
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trajectories"} trajectories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = [0,1]
            the closed
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval"} interval
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+leaves"} symplectic leaves
            are each a copy of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/source"} source
            term added.
          %p
            The first statement was first observed for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peierls+bracket"} Peierls bracket
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} local prequantum field theory
            in (
            %a{:href => "#Marolf93"}> Marolf 93, section II
            ), but the construction there is not specific to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peierls+bracket"} Peierls bracket
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation"} foliation
            of trajectory space by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+leaves"} symplectic leaves
            labeled by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+sets"} level sets
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+equation"} Euler-Lagrange function
            was explicitly pointed out at (
            %a{:href => "#BrunettiFredenhagenRibeiro12"}> Brunetti-Fredenhagen-Ribeiro 12, top of p. 4
            ). (Again for the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peierls+bracket"} Peierls bracket
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/source"} source
            terms was highlighted out by (
            %a{:href => "#Khavkine13"}> Khavkine 13
            ).
          %h2#on_paths_in_a_symplectic_manifold On paths in a symplectic manifold
          %p
            We describe here the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/off-shell"} off-shell
            Poisson bracket in the context of
